sequenceDiagram
    participant Caller as caller (endpoint or orchestrator)
    participant X as Exchange
    participant R as Registry
    participant N as Connector
    participant Callee as callee endpoint
    participant Q as Callee's queue
    participant L as Ledger

    Caller->>X: dial(to, verb, artifact.type)
    X->>R: resolve(to)
    R-->>X: transport (profile + locator) + org
    X->>N: dial offer
    N->>Callee: OFFER {caller, verb, artifact.type}
    alt accept
        Callee-->>N: accept
        N-->>X: accepted
        X->>Q: enqueue envelope
        X->>L: record offer=accepted, session open
    else decline (or timeout = implicit decline)
        Callee-->>N: decline / (silence)
        N-->>X: declined
        X->>L: record offer=declined
        X-->>Caller: declined
    else defer (endpoint or its host signals backpressure)
        Callee-->>N: defer (retry-after) / HTTP 429
        N-->>X: deferred (retry-after)
        X->>L: record offer=deferred, retry scheduled
    end

    note over X,Callee: Endpoints with no acceptance webhook get a<br/>console-configured default the Exchange evaluates<br/>on their behalf — the only way humans are reachable.
